---
source: crates/oxc_formatter_yaml/tests/fixtures/mod.rs
---
==================== Input ====================
# `sortOpenapi.components: true` orders the members of every direct member of the root `components`
# mapping alphabetically. Off by default.
#
# It is the children of `components.<type>` that move, not `components`' own entries -- those are
# ordered by the `components` table either way. So `schemas` keeps its table position while `Zebra`,
# `alpha` and `Beta` inside it are reordered.
#
# Alphabetical here means the key comparator: case-insensitive, so `alpha` precedes `Beta` precedes
# `Zebra`. Contrast `paths-path`, which is case-sensitive.
#
# `parameters` shows the precedence: its key has a table, and rule 1 beats the alphabetical pass, so it
# comes out in table order (`name`, `in`, ...) rather than alphabetically. Verified against the
# reference, which yields [name, in, schema, aaa, zzz].
openapi: 3.0.0
components:
  schemas:
    Zebra: {}
    alpha: {}
    Beta: {}
  responses:
    zzz: {}
    aaa: {}
  parameters:
    zzz: x
    schema: s
    name: n
    aaa: y
    in: query

==================== Output ====================
----------------------------------------------------
{ printWidth: 80, sortOpenapi: {"components":true} }
----------------------------------------------------
# `sortOpenapi.components: true` orders the members of every direct member of the root `components`
# mapping alphabetically. Off by default.
#
# It is the children of `components.<type>` that move, not `components`' own entries -- those are
# ordered by the `components` table either way. So `schemas` keeps its table position while `Zebra`,
# `alpha` and `Beta` inside it are reordered.
#
# Alphabetical here means the key comparator: case-insensitive, so `alpha` precedes `Beta` precedes
# `Zebra`. Contrast `paths-path`, which is case-sensitive.
#
# `parameters` shows the precedence: its key has a table, and rule 1 beats the alphabetical pass, so it
# comes out in table order (`name`, `in`, ...) rather than alphabetically. Verified against the
# reference, which yields [name, in, schema, aaa, zzz].
openapi: 3.0.0
components:
  parameters:
    name: n
    in: query
    schema: s
    aaa: y
    zzz: x
  schemas:
    alpha: {}
    Beta: {}
    Zebra: {}
  responses:
    aaa: {}
    zzz: {}

